 "summary_short": {
  "hook": "Richer than America. Then it went broke.",
  "say": "In the nineteen seventies, a tiny Pacific island called Nauru was richer per person than the United States. It was sitting on one of the purest phosphate deposits ever found. No taxes. Free hospitals. Its own airline. A skyscraper in Melbourne. Then the mines dug out eighty percent of the island. The money went into bad loans, a failed London musical, and banks that laundered billions. By two thousand five, its last plane was seized. Today, most of Nauru is dead grey stone. The full story is on the channel.",
